A.A_=s(["MAX \u20b9/kg is the most you may pay per kg so that, after mandi commission, hamali, your share of the trip charges and your own shrink, the retail rate you entered still leaves your margin.","MAX \u20b9/crate is that ceiling times one crate's net weight.","Max kg is what you expect to sell before your next trip, grossed up for your own shrink. Crates is the whole crates inside it \u2014 what you actually buy.","Every per-kg cost is (your share of the charges) \xf7 (crates \xd7 crate weight), not \xf7 the plan weight, because a mandi sells crates.","Break-even is the same calculation with your margin set to zero. A dash means there is no break-even to print \u2014 that row is below zero before your margin is counted.","A ceiling holds only at the crate count printed on its own row. Buy fewer crates and the same trip charges spread over fewer kg, so the real ceiling is lower."],t.s)
