A.aDL=s(["Amaranth leaves","Ash gourd","Beetroot","Bitter gourd","Bottle gourd","Brinjal","Broad beans","Cabbage","Capsicum","Carrot","Cauliflower","Cluster beans","Colocasia","Coriander","Cucumber","Curry leaves","Dill leaves","Drumstick","Elephant-foot yam","Fenugreek leaves","French beans","Garlic","Ginger","Green chilli","Green peas","Ivy gourd","Mint","Okra","Onion","Potato","Pumpkin","Radish","Raw banana","Ridge gourd","Snake gourd","Spinach","Spring onion","Sweet potato","Tinda","Tomato"],t.s)
A.Ak=s(["A mandi auction is a live competitive bid, and you have to come home with stock. This card is a reference, not a rule. If the bidding goes past your number you may still be right to take it \u2014 you will just know exactly what it is costing you.","Every figure comes from numbers YOU typed. boliseema has no rate data, no market data and no internet at runtime. It cannot tell you what anything is worth today.","The retail rate is what you think you can get, not what you will get. The low\u2013high band is there so the card shows you how fast the ceiling moves when that judgement is wrong.","Your retail rate is not independent of the auction. Everyone in your lane bought at the same hammer, so on a day when the mandi runs hot the retail rate moves up with it \u2014 and a ceiling worked out from last week's retail rate is then too low, not too high. This card holds the retail rate you typed still; the market does not.","Shrink, cull and wastage are your own percentage. We ship 0% and a 25 kg placeholder crate \u2014 both are placeholders, not measurements. Weigh your crate.","Days until your next trip is your judgement. We have no data for how long anything keeps on a cart in an Indian summer, and we are not going to pretend we do. Leave it blank and the card will not print.","The maximum kg is the most to bring home, not a purchase order. It assumes you sell at your typical daily rate every day until your next trip. A festival, a wedding street, or rain makes it wrong.","Trip charges are split across vegetables by crate space, which is an assumption about your tempo, not a fact about your costs. It is stated on the card so you can argue with it.","A mandi sells crates, not kilograms. Every per-kg cost is therefore divided by the whole crates that fit inside your plan weight \u2014 not by the plan weight itself \u2014 and the hamali is charged on those crates. The leftover kg that do not make a whole crate are named on the row rather than quietly bought.","Rounding always goes the safe way: costs round up, the maximum bid and the maximum kg round down, so the rounding is never optimistic \u2014 it may cost you a paisa or two. The ceiling itself is only true AT THE CRATE COUNT PRINTED ON ITS OWN ROW. Come home with fewer crates and the same trip charges spread over fewer kg, so the real ceiling is lower than the one on this card. On a 5-crate row, buying 3 makes the printed number about 7% too high.","boliseema is not accounting, not a ledger, not a credit book, and not tax advice.","Local-first: your data is a SQLite file on your machine. The app runs on localhost. There are no accounts, no sync, no encryption, and nothing leaves your device. The Pages demo stores nothing server-side and forgets everything on refresh."],t.s)
